# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# Enviroments
*.env

# Compiled output
/dist
/tmp
/out-tsc
/bazel-out

# public/ IS NOT IGNORED, and that is deliberate — do not re-add it.
#
# `public/img` and `public/mock` used to be generated copies of ../design/photos
# and ../jsons/landing, regenerated by scripts/sync-assets.mjs through the npm
# pre-hooks. That made the deployable app depend on two folders that are NOT in
# this repository: a clone, a CI runner or a `git archive` produced a build with
# no photographs in it, and nothing failed loudly — Angular simply copied an
# empty public/img and the landing rendered with broken image icons.
#
# Those files are now committed here and this repository is self-contained:
# what you clone is what deploys. Ignoring them again reintroduces exactly that
# failure.

